From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: disable RX NAPI only once

The native unregister path now disables all added RX NAPIs before MCU
exit and DMA cleanup. Keep that early disable owner and remove the local
registration-aware disable loop from the later DMA cleanup stage.
A second napi_disable() waits forever on the SCHED/NPSVC bits retained
by the first call. Registration tracking and partial-queue cleanup stay
unchanged, including the separate NPU queue teardown stage.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -1053,14 +1053,7 @@
 
 void mt7996_dma_cleanup(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
-	int i;
-
 	mt7996_dma_disable(dev, true);
 
-	/* Other mt76 drivers quiesce RX NAPI in their own remove paths. */
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->mt76.napi); i++)
-		if (test_bit(i, &dev->mt76.napi_registered))
-			napi_disable(&dev->mt76.napi[i]);
-
 	mt76_dma_cleanup(&dev->mt76);
 }
